// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL8_9_Issue7_Coop_Arc 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P1127666073" "View of Planet Earth"
// tDetailString :
"P1132309439" "In between your adventures, you sometimes remember the view you had of planet earth while on Darrin Wade's floating island. The planet as a whole looked beautiful and also small, in a way. The planet was in the background as you fought for its survival against a Darrin Wade in the last moments of an adventure you call...<br><br><b>To Something Greater</b><br><br>Where did this whole journey really begin? Was it with the first move by Darrin Wade to give the Lost an obelisk that would steal Synapse's powers? Or were these events that were set in motions thousands of years ago, back during the time of Cimerora? Wherever it started, you were the one who was destined to end it. Darrin Wade had gained the power of Statesman and Sister Psyche. He sought to summon Rularuu into this world and become one with the monster. You ended up working together with Arachnos to track Wade down. You travelled the globe and dimensions, going to the Shadow Shard to speak with Faathim the Kind, to the pacific ocean for your first encounter against Wade's floating island, and then Warburg, to retake it from Malta in order to destroy the shield around Wade's island.<br><br>You faced off against the transformed Darrin Wade in space, the fate of the world hanging in the balance. You defeated Wade, his mind being sent back to the husk that now is his body. You think back to how the world nearly came to the brink of destruction and the information that you gathered all this time, along with the help of Lady Grey...<br><br>It all began with Alastor, who had created a group of obelisks thousands of years ago to take power away from the gods and put it into the hands of the people. Sister Airlia played her part in Cimerora, where she wished to gain control over the country by having Imperious and Romulus destroyed. Centuries passed, leading to the present day. Darrin Wade, born a normal but extremely intelligent man, saw that no matter what he did, he could never be greater than the simplest of heroes. His life would always be dependent on those whom he believed were less than him. Jean-Pierre Lourdin, known as Malaise, was a twisted man who Sister Psyche was trying to heal. He desired to be free from Psyche, to have control over himself.<br><br>All of these people wanted to gain power and control to gain their own freedom. They were willing to do whatever it takes to do this, even if it meant killing whoever they needed to satisfy their dreams. Yet, in the end, all of them failed. Alastor's obelisks were either destroyed or never used by him, Sister Airlia, it can be presumed, never came to power, as the story of Cimerora was lost to the ages. Malaise was destroyed in Sister Psyche's mind, his actions bound to his desire for vengeance. Darrin Wade's mind is nearly mush now, trapped inside of his body. His freedom to move, to act, is gone, save for the most basic of actions.<br><br>The world is safe, but perhaps you wonder, what is the true idea of freedom that all these people wanted? Freedom must mean more than having the power to do whatever you wish. You think back to Statesman, who, in his final moments, was smiling. Could it be that in that moment, Darrin Wade, who had all the power, all the control, was the one who was a slave to his circumstances, while Statesman, in his final moments, was finally free from it all?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Scirocco 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Hero Text :
"P1418038769" "{HeroName}, know that I hold it against you for attacking Ghost Widow, but I am willing to put aside my issues to try to bargain with you. I am sure as a hero of Paragon, you're willing to do the same.<br><br>As you can tell, Ghost Widow and I have been investigating how to track down Darrin Wade. Recluse is not pleased about Statesman's death.<br><br>Now, understand that this isn't some sort of misguided brotherly love. Recluse wants Wade dead because he possesses the power of Statesman and can be a threat to his power.<br><br>I was returning here to report that I've been able to pick up on Darrin Wade's magical signature and track where he went last. You are, no doubt, extremely capable, given how much Wade has tried to kill you all of this time. I propose that we all work together in tracking Wade down. I have the information you need, and you have the power and nobility to follow this through to the end."
// Answer Text :
"P2405081071" "Of course I'll work together with you, but what about your master, Recluse?"
// Answer Text :
"P2486048743" "Forget it, I should take you in here and now for your crimes!"
// Page HeroChoice1Page1 Text :
"P2102057228" "Lord Recluse will have to deal with the fact that there is a hero working with us. We are all well aware that the major forces of the world are currently spread very thin.<br><br>It's ironic, really, that it has come down to Arachnos having the most interest and organization in pulling together to track down Darrin Wade, even if Recluse's own goals aren't as altruistic as one would hope.<br><br>I should warn you, {HeroName}, to not be too trusting of the organization. Recluse will do what it takes to end Wade, but if I know him, he will not hesitate to try to take you out as well, should the opportunity present itself. I will, unfortunately, have to follow through and aid him, should the order be given to me."
// Answer Text :
"P1777816944" "I understand. What information do you have?"
// Page HeroChoice1FinalPage Text :
"P215130264" "Yes, of course. Darrin Wade's signature fluctuated back and forth to various parts of the globe before suddenly vanishing. I've spoken with Operative Grillo and we've identified where his signature went; the Shadow Shard.<br><br>It makes sense, really, given all of his dealings with Rularuu. From what we could tell, he went to the Chantry, the place where Faathim the Kind resides.<br><br>I'll be heading there shortly to do what I can to track him down. I assume that I will see you in there."
// Answer Text :
"P889116695" "You will."
// Page HeroChoice3Page1 Text :
"P2401980832" "<color orange>Scirocco holds his hands up at your words.</color><br><br>Perhaps you should, {HeroName}. I've done many horrible crimes in the past, and I most likely will continue to do so. However, out of all the patrons you could be speaking to, I would nominate myself to be the most trustworthy.<br><br>I want nothing more than to stop Darrin Wade from taking over the world as Rularuu; believe me, I have had my proposals for changing the world, and having Wade rule it is not one of them.<br><br>If you wish to arrest me, there will be plenty of chances for you to do so afterwards. Right now, however, myself and Arachnos are your best chance at tracking down Wade, as much as that must boil your blood."
// Answer Text :
"P2954358830" "I'm keeping my eye on you, Scirocco. What information do you have?"
// Answer Text :
"P2871846290" "I'll be there, Scirocco, don't you worry about that."
// Page Villain Text :
"P3481128464" "{HeroName}. I should've known you'd be here. Is Vanguard actually allowing you to help them? They're quite the forgiving organization, aren't they? I suppose when you want to get results, you go to the best.<br><br>I should strike you down here and now for attacking Ghost Widow, but I understand you most likely would be able to best me, much like you've bested Darrin Wade's attempts at defeating you.<br><br>You are looking for Wade, much like we are in Arachnos. I would propose that we merge our two goals together to get this task accomplished. I understand you may have a rather sordid history with Arachnos, but I can assure you that we only seek to destroy Wade utterly in all of this.<br><br>I have the information needed to track him down, but I need to know that you're willing to work together with Arachnos to do this."
// Answer Text :
"P1099941623" "Fine, we'll work together. Just tell Recluse this doesn't make me his lackey."
// Answer Text :
"P3827020441" "Lower myself to working for Arachnos? You can forget about it."
// Page VillainChoice1Page1 Text :
"P672762697" "Of course, {HeroName}. You are not tied directly to the organization like I am. There is no 'lackey' title being thrown about.<br><br>Arachnos could use all the help it could get, as I understand it. We are the last major organized force who is available to go against Darrin Wade. As we speak, monsters of Rularuu are appearing all over the world. Vanguard is fighting them off, while the United Nations have requested the presence of Longbow and even the Paragon Police Department to travel abroad to help.<br><br>Lord Recluse has ordered the soldiers of Arachnos to fortify the defenses within Grandville and Cap au Diable, leaving only the patrons, himself, and a select few Bane Spiders left to handle this."
// Answer Text :
"P3007227295" "Alright. You said you knew where Wade was."
// Page VillainChoice1FinalPage Text :
"P1908409238" "I do. Darrin Wade's signature fluctuated back and forth to various parts of the globe before suddenly vanishing. I've spoken with Operative Grillo and we've identified where his signature went; the Shadow Shard.<br><br>It makes sense, really, given all of his dealings with Rularuu. From what we could tell, he went to the Chantry, the place where Faathim the Kind resides.<br><br>I'll be heading there shortly to do what I can to track him down. I assume I will see you there shortly, {HeroName}."
// Answer Text :
"P3936123470" "Alright."
// Page VillainChoice3Page1 Text :
"P4248551643" "You aren't working for us, {HeroName}. We would be working together, as equals. Recluse may not admit it, but I am willing to, if it means saving the world.<br><br>I am sure you have your own plans and devices for working this out in your favor. Whatever they are, they will require that we both work together. There are precious few people left in the world who have the attention to deal with this situation. You are one of them, along with the higher ups within Arachnos.<br><br>We must all pull together if we're to stop Darrin Wade from destroying everything."
// Answer Text :
"P1545445782" "Alright, fine, for the 'greater good' as usual. Where's Darrin Wade?"
// Page VillainChoice3FinalPage Text :
"P3342272168" "Darrin Wade's signature fluctuated back and forth to various parts of the globe before suddenly vanishing. I've spoken with Operative Grillo and we've identified where his signature went; the Shadow Shard.<br><br>It makes sense, really, given all of his dealings with Rularuu. From what we could tell, he went to the Chantry, the place where Faathim the Kind resides.<br><br>I'll be heading there shortly to do what I can to track him down. I assume I will see you there shortly, {HeroName}."
// Page PatronVillain Text :
"P228363048" "You always seem to show up to interfere with our plans, {HeroName}. We're trying to <i>save</i> the world here, much like I was trying to save it with the Malleus Mundi. Yet, you feel the need to stop my efforts at every turn.<br><br>I'm assuming you're with Vanguard, which means you still are somehow <i>trying</i> to save the world, though I am certain it is only for your own selfish ends.<br><br>As much as it pains me to say this, I believe you and I are fated to work together in this endeavor. You've foiled Darrin Wade at every turn thus far, which would make you the one person who he has targeted who hasn't been killed. I have the information required to actually track Wade's location. Arachnos and, regretabbly, myself, will help by providing our manpower and information, while you help by foiling someone else's plans. That is, after all, what you seem to excel in."
// Answer Text :
"P3535498340" "If you're willing to be civil, we can do this."
// Answer Text :
"P1482576975" "You were going to enslave me and the world, Scirocco. What was I supposed to do?"
// Page PatronVillainChoice1Page1 Text :
"P3486395939" "I am perfectly willing to be civil, {HeroName}. You showed me that happens when I try to branch out on my own to change the world for the better.<br><br>Recluse wishes to see Wade stopped, which is why I am allowed to do what I can to stop him. So yes, I am willing to be civil, as I'm being allowed to do my part to protect this world. I'll be keeping my eye on you, however, as I fully suspect that you will try to turn on us."
// Answer Text :
"P109857120" "Of course. Where is Wade now?"
// Page PatronVillainChoice3Page1 Text :
"P3661498798" "It would not have been enslavement, {HeroName}, it would have been changing the world to be <i>better</i>. I was willing to sacrifice myself to be exiled from such a world, only if I could have made it a reality... why would you not be so noble as to do the same?<br><br>... Regardless, my failing is in the past. We now face a new threat of Darrin Wade, who is willing to enslave the world to his own whims. Unlike myself, he seeks only to benefit himself."
// Answer Text :
"P776849621" "You're both very different, of course. Where is he now?"
// Page PatronHero Text :
"P1451729225" "{HeroName}. My former pupil gone hero. It seems you've accomplished something that I could never hope to achieve, but that is neither here nor there. Know that I hold it against you for attacking Ghost Widow, but I am willing to put aside my issues to try to bargain with you. <br><br>As you can tell, Ghost Widow and I have been investigating how to track down Darrin Wade. Recluse is not pleased about Statesman's death.<br><br>Now, understand that this isn't some sort of misguided brotherly love. Recluse wants Wade dead because he possesses the power of Statesman and can be a threat to his power.<br><br>I was returning here to report that I've been able to pick up on Darrin Wade's magical signature and track where he went last. You are, no doubt, extremely capable, given how much Wade has tried to kill you all of this time. I propose that we all work together in tracking Wade down. I have the information you need, and you have the power and nobility to follow this through to the end."
// Answer Text :
"P1242185565" "Scirocco, it's not too late for you to change your ways, just like I did."
// Answer Text :
"P1525671316" "No, Scirocco, I should take you in here and now for your crimes!"
// Page PatronHeroChoice2Page1 Text :
"P576734871" "<color orange>Scirocco lets out a slight smile, shaking his head.</color><br><br>You are not tied to Arachnos as much as I am, {HeroName}. If I were to leave, unspeakable things would happen. As well... where would I go? Perhaps there are those who would accept you, but I have disgraced my family name and those who I fought together with during the old war.<br><br>No person would accept me after what I've done. The only option is to continue moving forward with where I am. That is the only thing I <i>can</i> do, {HeroName}. The question now is what you are going to do next."
// Answer Text :
"P386063409" "I'll work with you, but what about Recluse?"
// Answer Text :
"P4117966696" "I cannot work with you, Scirocco. You need to pay for your crimes."
// Page PatronHeroChoice3Page1 Text :
"P2110328859" "<color orange>Scirocco holds his hands up at your words.</color><br><br>Perhaps you should, {HeroName}. I've done many horrible crimes in the past, and I most likely will continue to do so. However, out of all the patrons you could be speaking to, I would nominate myself to be the most trustworthy. Surely you know that as well as I do.<br><br>I want nothing more than to stop Darrin Wade from taking over the world as Rularuu; believe me, I have had my proposals for changing the world, and having Wade rule it is not one of them.<br><br>If you wish to arrest me, there will be plenty of chances for you to do so afterwards. Right now, however, myself and Arachnos are your best chance at tracking down Wade, as much as that must boil your blood."
// Answer Text :
"P2559484788" "Finish"

